WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club

﻿1

00:03:50.814 --> 00:03:51.814
Hey.


00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:41.615
Colonel, give us
the room, please.


00:04:49.331 --> 00:04:51.958
Four years retired
yet two salutes?


00:04:51.959 --> 00:04:54.336
- Shows respect.
- Have a seat.


00:04:58.715 --> 00:04:59.967
Do you know who I am?


00:05:00.717 --> 00:05:02.009
No.


00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.428
Well, if you were to guess.


00:05:06.056 --> 00:05:07.890
Judging by your age, appearance,


00:05:07.891 --> 00:05:11.019
and how a Marine colonel just
followed your order without a yip,


00:05:11.854 --> 00:05:14.106
I'd guess you're some
kind of high-level spook.


00:05:19.027 --> 00:05:21.530
Your father and
grandfather served?


00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:23.322
Yes.


00:05:23.991 --> 00:05:27.952
As an elite sniper, you
have 113 confirmed kills


00:05:27.953 --> 00:05:30.705
and an additional
81 probable kills.


00:05:30.706 --> 00:05:32.124
Are those numbers accurate?


00:05:32.624 --> 00:05:33.624
No.


00:05:34.042 --> 00:05:37.421
- Are the actual numbers fewer or greater?
- Greater.


00:05:38.755 --> 00:05:41.674
As a veteran, how many private
contractors have you worked for?


00:05:41.675 --> 00:05:42.592
Eleven.


00:05:42.593 --> 00:05:45.721
But you also still work for
the Marine Corps on occasion?


00:05:47.055 --> 00:05:48.389
Anytime they call.


00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:52.269
And are you presently under any
private or military contract?


00:05:54.146 --> 00:05:55.146
No.


00:05:57.191 --> 00:05:59.443
You're an extremely
rare talent, Levi.


00:06:00.944 --> 00:06:01.944
Why not?


00:06:04.239 --> 00:06:07.450
In June, some corporate shrink told
me that I was unfit for a mission,


00:06:07.451 --> 00:06:09.243
but I'm sure you
already know that.


00:06:09.244 --> 00:06:10.537
So why are you asking me?


00:06:13.624 --> 00:06:15.416
Do you think you're
fit for service?


00:06:15.417 --> 00:06:16.960
Doesn't matter what I think.


00:06:19.796 --> 00:06:22.048
So, do you presently
have a girlfriend?


00:06:22.049 --> 00:06:23.300
Anyone special?


00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.011
Someone who couldn't
live without you?


00:06:28.889 --> 00:06:30.349
- No.
- Why not?


00:06:31.517 --> 00:06:33.060
Just not how it goes for me.


00:06:35.187 --> 00:06:39.315
How about meds,
illegal drugs, alcohol?


00:06:39.316 --> 00:06:40.651
No drugs.


00:06:41.443 --> 00:06:42.568
But if I time it right,


00:06:42.569 --> 00:06:45.989
three and a half ounces of booze right
before I go to bed helps with the dreams.


00:06:46.698 --> 00:06:50.201
Have you tried
Nitrazepam or Prazosin?


00:06:50.202 --> 00:06:52.037
Have you ever killed
someone at long range?


00:06:55.624 --> 00:06:57.084
Pills affect my accuracy.


00:07:00.629 --> 00:07:05.049
Levi, you could have contested the
psych test and seen another doctor.


00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:06.050
Why didn't you?


00:07:06.468 --> 00:07:07.593
I had no reason to.


00:07:07.594 --> 00:07:09.054
You had no reason?


00:07:10.973 --> 00:07:13.642
There's not a lot of
reasons for me right now.


00:07:19.606 --> 00:07:20.983
What if I gave you a reason?


00:07:43.463 --> 00:07:44.463
Hey, Daddy.


00:07:57.603 --> 00:07:58.603
To music.


00:07:59.188 --> 00:08:00.856
To music.


00:08:02.191 --> 00:08:04.483
My Little Lion...


00:08:04.484 --> 00:08:05.651
How are you?


00:08:05.652 --> 00:08:06.652
You know.


00:08:07.237 --> 00:08:08.405
Better now I see you.


00:08:08.906 --> 00:08:13.452
There is a rumor you were
photographed in Belarus.


00:08:14.369 --> 00:08:16.412
A drone.


00:08:16.413 --> 00:08:18.123
Is that possible?


00:08:18.832 --> 00:08:24.171
Moscow cannot risk having a direct
link to the oligarch's death.


00:08:29.134 --> 00:08:30.511
He had four children.


00:08:33.013 --> 00:08:34.014
Give it to me.


00:08:36.099 --> 00:08:37.308
Give me your shame.


00:08:52.908 --> 00:08:58.455
The Belarusian made himself rich trading
in white phosphorus bombs and land mines.


00:08:59.915 --> 00:09:01.875
How many children's
legs were lost?


00:09:02.459 --> 00:09:06.380
How many little faces were forever
burnt by those transactions?


00:09:08.882 --> 00:09:10.634
You give the shame to me...


00:09:17.099 --> 00:09:18.392
And you move forward.


00:09:19.434 --> 00:09:20.811
It's not so easy anymore.


00:09:22.855 --> 00:09:23.856
I don't sleep.


00:09:25.399 --> 00:09:26.482
Sometimes for days.


00:09:26.483 --> 00:09:29.987
Stay with me for a week or two.


00:09:31.029 --> 00:09:34.407
And we'll make a stew. It
would be good for both of us.


00:09:34.408 --> 00:09:35.408
I can't.


00:09:36.285 --> 00:09:39.328
Rabinovich has ordered me to a briefing
first thing tomorrow morning in Moscow.


00:09:39.329 --> 00:09:41.581
To hell with Rabinovich,
and to hell with Moscow.


00:09:41.582 --> 00:09:43.416
You're not Russian,
you're Lithuanian.


00:09:43.417 --> 00:09:46.628
He says I'll be going
dark for at least a year.


00:09:47.796 --> 00:09:48.796
Perhaps more.


00:09:51.258 --> 00:09:52.258
Hey.


00:09:52.926 --> 00:09:55.094
Did you go to the doctor
I arranged for you?


00:09:55.095 --> 00:09:56.012
The specialist?


00:09:56.013 --> 00:09:58.098
- Yes, I did.
- And?


00:09:58.974 --> 00:10:00.600
There's nothing to be done.


00:10:00.601 --> 00:10:02.102
Look at me, I'm a wretch.


00:10:02.686 --> 00:10:04.813
Cancer eats me from
the inside out.


00:10:05.397 --> 00:10:07.482
Liver, pancreas.


00:10:08.483 --> 00:10:10.485
Death will be a welcome change.


00:10:10.986 --> 00:10:12.487
And what if I'm not back?


00:10:14.323 --> 00:10:17.910
You'll be alone, and I won't
even know when it happens.


00:10:19.036 --> 00:10:20.370
An easy solution.


00:10:21.163 --> 00:10:22.581
I've already decided.


00:10:23.373 --> 00:10:26.167
February 14th, Valentine's Day.


00:10:26.168 --> 00:10:27.248
What are you talking about?


00:10:27.836 --> 00:10:29.463
I'm going to do it myself.


00:10:30.088 --> 00:10:32.089
Assuming I'm not
already dead, of course.


00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:33.175
Dad.


00:10:36.345 --> 00:10:38.180
- Dad, you're not...
- It's my life to take.


00:10:39.598 --> 00:10:43.060
I will be ready to finally
rest here next to your mother.


00:10:45.020 --> 00:10:49.982
So, wherever you are, you
light a candle for me,


00:10:49.983 --> 00:10:53.570
you look at the Hunter in the
night sky, then you'll know.


00:10:57.324 --> 00:10:59.785
Come on now, Little Lion.


00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:01.954
Let's have our beer,


00:11:02.829 --> 00:11:03.829
play a song,


00:11:05.082 --> 00:11:06.917
and say a proper goodbye.


00:12:03.015 --> 00:12:04.725
Place your left hand on the pad.


00:12:10.105 --> 00:12:12.482
Put your watch, your smart
phone, and your ID in the case.


00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:14.526
It just tells time.


00:12:19.448 --> 00:12:21.866
In three minutes, we reach
the edge of the no-fly zone.


00:12:21.867 --> 00:12:23.368
That's as far as
we can take you.


00:12:23.994 --> 00:12:26.371
From the drop, you'll have
another 38 klicks north on foot.


00:12:27.164 --> 00:12:29.290
You're expected by
1600 hours tomorrow.


00:12:29.291 --> 00:12:30.709
Open it on the ground.


00:12:37.299 --> 00:12:38.717
Where are we?


00:12:39.801 --> 00:12:41.386
I'm not authorized
to answer that.


00:14:07.097 --> 00:14:09.892
At long last, my
sweet prince has come.


00:14:10.642 --> 00:14:13.896
Punctual even. Spot
on time. What a guy.


00:14:14.897 --> 00:14:18.858
Jasper D. Drake, Royal Marines
Commandos. Just call me JD.


00:14:18.859 --> 00:14:21.986
Levi Kane, former US
Marine, scout sniper.


00:14:21.987 --> 00:14:23.154
Mercenary?


00:14:23.155 --> 00:14:24.531
Private contractor.


00:14:25.032 --> 00:14:26.616
So, what did they tell
you about this mission?


00:14:26.617 --> 00:14:27.868
Not a damn thing.


00:14:28.702 --> 00:14:30.578
They gave me an
unmarked topo map.


00:14:30.579 --> 00:14:31.996
I don't even know
what country I'm in.


00:14:31.997 --> 00:14:34.666
I've been here an entire year
and I have no idea where I am.


00:14:35.167 --> 00:14:36.335
It's messed up, right?


00:14:36.835 --> 00:14:39.213
But that is just the
tippity-top of the iceberg.


00:14:40.839 --> 00:14:42.632
Man, am I glad to see you.


00:14:42.633 --> 00:14:43.966
Not a lot of contact, huh?


00:14:43.967 --> 00:14:47.012
You're the first person I've
spoken to face-to-face in a year.


00:14:47.721 --> 00:14:49.139
You're all alone out here?


00:14:49.681 --> 00:14:52.017
And my tour rotation
officially ends at midnight.


00:14:52.809 --> 00:14:54.685
- So I'm the relief?
- Affirmative.


00:14:54.686 --> 00:14:57.064
Look, we'll get a drink and
I'll explain everything.


00:14:58.190 --> 00:14:59.316
There she is.


00:14:59.942 --> 00:15:01.526
West Tower Observation Post.


00:15:01.527 --> 00:15:04.321
Your home away from home
for the next 365 days.


00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:09.575
Completely self-sufficient, solar
with a generator backup, rain system,


00:15:09.576 --> 00:15:12.871
wild game is plentiful, and
there's a garden right there.


00:15:13.455 --> 00:15:14.581
Everything you need.


00:15:15.415 --> 00:15:16.615
What's that on the other side?


00:15:18.293 --> 00:15:19.836
That is East Tower.


00:15:19.837 --> 00:15:21.754
Contact with the other
side is strictly forbidden,


00:15:21.755 --> 00:15:25.091
which is irrelevant given the land
mines and lethal tactical barriers


00:15:25.092 --> 00:15:26.801
to the north and
south of the Gorge.


00:15:26.802 --> 00:15:28.594
Can't get to the
other side anyway.


00:15:28.595 --> 00:15:30.680
In practical terms, East
Tower is not an issue.


00:15:30.681 --> 00:15:32.724
They do their
thing. You do yours.


00:15:33.225 --> 00:15:35.727
I did see movement over that
side earlier this morning.


00:15:36.311 --> 00:15:38.564
Think they just completed
their annual rotation too.


00:15:39.231 --> 00:15:40.982
Theoretically, the job's simple.


00:15:40.983 --> 00:15:42.483
You're not the principal
line of defense.


00:15:42.484 --> 00:15:45.486
You're more like a highly
skilled maintenance man.


00:15:45.487 --> 00:15:47.446
Every day, you walk
the western rim.


00:15:47.447 --> 00:15:50.450
There are automatic Phalanx gun
turrets every 600 meters or so.


00:15:50.951 --> 00:15:52.660
You restock the ammo
in the auto gun,


00:15:52.661 --> 00:15:55.955
check the containment fence,
cloakers and suspended mines.


00:15:55.956 --> 00:16:00.001
There's an armory in the bunker outside.
Weapons, tools, replacement ammo, mines.


00:16:00.002 --> 00:16:01.086
Whatever you need.


00:16:02.087 --> 00:16:03.881
Radio check every 30 days.


00:16:04.548 --> 00:16:05.882
What's a cloaker?


00:16:05.883 --> 00:16:08.134
Cloaker is a type of
satellite transmitter.


00:16:08.135 --> 00:16:10.261
There's one every kilometer
or so along the rim,


00:16:10.262 --> 00:16:14.182
each with its own power
and backup power source.


00:16:14.183 --> 00:16:16.393
- What do they do?
- They cloak.


00:16:17.436 --> 00:16:19.353
They send a false signal
to all the satellites


00:16:19.354 --> 00:16:20.856
that pass overhead
on a given day.


00:16:21.398 --> 00:16:24.442
They're designed to render the
Gorge invisible to spy satellites,


00:16:24.443 --> 00:16:26.283
but they also work with
shit like Google Earth.


00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:31.115
There is no outside
communication here.


00:16:31.116 --> 00:16:32.910
No cell, no sat, no nothing.


00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:35.411
In case of an emergency,
there's a panic button


00:16:35.412 --> 00:16:38.581
on the dedicated shortwave radio
you use for monthly radio checks.


00:16:38.582 --> 00:16:40.541
Button triggers a signal,
which lets them know that...


00:16:40.542 --> 00:16:41.543
Let's who know?


00:16:42.586 --> 00:16:44.545
The powers that be, mate.


00:16:44.546 --> 00:16:45.546
Whoever.


00:16:46.048 --> 00:16:48.509
Did you spy the old air-raid
sirens atop the tower?


00:16:49.259 --> 00:16:53.387
If, somehow, all the cloakers fail at
once or if the Gorge is ever overrun,


00:16:53.388 --> 00:16:57.099
their automated system executes
something called a Straydog protocol.


00:16:57.100 --> 00:16:58.768
Straydog protocol.


00:16:58.769 --> 00:17:00.145
- What is that?
- No idea.


00:17:00.687 --> 00:17:03.899
But if you hear those air-raid
sirens, you run like hell.


00:17:05.192 --> 00:17:06.275
Copy that.


00:17:06.276 --> 00:17:07.860
Look, here's the deal.


00:17:07.861 --> 00:17:09.154
This place is old.


00:17:09.863 --> 00:17:12.323
I'm talking end of the Second
World War, early Cold War shit.


00:17:12.324 --> 00:17:13.783
And it's secret.


00:17:13.784 --> 00:17:15.535
Way back then, an
agreement was made,


00:17:15.536 --> 00:17:17.787
and a coalition formed
to keep it a secret.


00:17:17.788 --> 00:17:20.914
So, now, every year, a new representative
from one of the western nations


00:17:20.915 --> 00:17:24.418
patrols the western rim and someone on
the other side patrols the eastern rim.


00:17:24.419 --> 00:17:25.503
They're your counterpart.


00:17:26.755 --> 00:17:28.631
You're telling me leaders
from the East and West


00:17:28.632 --> 00:17:31.008
have been secretly working
together for the last 75 years?


00:17:31.009 --> 00:17:35.471
No. I'm telling you there have been
nine Soviet Russian heads of state


00:17:35.472 --> 00:17:38.183
and 13 US presidents since
the coalitions were formed.


00:17:38.767 --> 00:17:40.567
And not one of them has
known about the Gorge.


00:17:41.019 --> 00:17:42.020
Give that a spin.


00:17:47.067 --> 00:17:49.403
Potato vodka. The
still is in the armory.


00:17:51.196 --> 00:17:52.196
That's good.


00:17:53.532 --> 00:17:56.293
The recipe's been passed down for
decades. So please don't mess it up.


00:17:58.537 --> 00:18:01.582
Listen, I'm sorry, man. But I just
feel like I'm missing something.


00:18:02.082 --> 00:18:05.794
So apart from keeping this place
a secret, what's the mission?


00:18:07.004 --> 00:18:08.671
I need to keep people
from going in the Gorge?


00:18:08.672 --> 00:18:09.672
No.


00:18:10.674 --> 00:18:13.552
You need to stop what's in
the Gorge from coming out.


00:18:16.305 --> 00:18:19.974
A year ago, I was in your boots and my
predecessor gave me the exact same speech.


00:18:19.975 --> 00:18:21.435
And what did I think of him?


00:18:22.769 --> 00:18:25.314
- That he's completely full of shit.
- Exactly.


00:18:26.064 --> 00:18:28.316
But trust me, keep your eyes
on the central Gorge walls.


00:18:28.317 --> 00:18:29.567
They're the most scalable.


00:18:29.568 --> 00:18:32.153
Sensor miniguns further north and
south should take care of the rest.


00:18:32.154 --> 00:18:33.739
Scale wh... Take care of what?


00:18:43.582 --> 00:18:44.666
What the hell is that?


00:18:45.167 --> 00:18:47.377
That is what we
call the Hollow Men.


00:18:47.961 --> 00:18:49.712
Nobody knows exactly
what they are.


00:18:49.713 --> 00:18:51.924
I don't even know why
they're called that.


00:18:52.424 --> 00:18:56.260
- It's the name of a T.S. Eliot poem.
- I don't know anything about that.


00:18:56.261 --> 00:18:59.388
All I know is that someone who had our
job called them that a long time ago


00:18:59.389 --> 00:19:00.474
and the name stuck.


00:19:01.391 --> 00:19:03.726
What I can tell you
is in the late 1940s,


00:19:03.727 --> 00:19:06.187
they sent three
entire battalions,


00:19:06.188 --> 00:19:09.149
2,400 men on horseback, into
the Gorge to clean it out.


00:19:09.816 --> 00:19:11.360
Not a single man returned.


00:19:12.027 --> 00:19:14.780
After that, they shifted to a
purely containment strategy.


00:19:16.365 --> 00:19:18.491
- How do you know all this?
- Same way you do.


00:19:18.492 --> 00:19:20.034
We're all briefed
by our predecessor.


00:19:20.035 --> 00:19:23.371
- Okay, so this could be one...
- A decades-long game of telephone.


00:19:23.372 --> 00:19:24.372
Yeah.


00:19:27.751 --> 00:19:30.712
JD, what do you think's
really going on here?


00:19:31.296 --> 00:19:35.300
Well, the theory I think summarizes
the situation most succinctly


00:19:36.677 --> 00:19:41.682
is the Gorge is the door to hell and
we're standing guard at the gate.


00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:49.648
- Take care of yourself.
- Good luck, man.


00:22:05.868 --> 00:22:07.660
Man, am I happy to see you.


00:22:07.661 --> 00:22:08.786
Right on, brother!


00:22:08.787 --> 00:22:12.290
I need you to quickly
confirm your identity.


00:22:12.291 --> 00:22:15.793
Jasper D. Drake.
Countersign: blue arrow.


00:22:15.794 --> 00:22:17.546
Thank you for your service.


00:22:28.557 --> 00:22:30.141
<i>Rotation complete.</i>


00:22:30.142 --> 00:22:31.310
Copy that.


00:23:41.880 --> 00:23:43.840
<i>This is West Tower
performing radio check.</i>


00:23:43.841 --> 00:23:44.925
Do you copy?


00:23:47.135 --> 00:23:49.428
I repeat, this is West Tower
performing radio check.


00:23:49.429 --> 00:23:50.972
Do you copy? Over.


00:23:50.973 --> 00:23:52.808
<i>Authentication code?</i>


00:23:53.809 --> 00:23:56.103
Alpha, Bravo,
nine, seven, Omega.


00:23:56.979 --> 00:23:59.438
- <i>Enemy contact?</i>
- Negative.


00:23:59.439 --> 00:24:00.774
<i>Cloaker status?</i>


00:24:01.275 --> 00:24:02.358
Green.


00:24:02.359 --> 00:24:03.777
<i>Procedure is complete.</i>


00:24:04.319 --> 00:24:05.863
<i>30 days until next radio check.</i>


00:24:06.363 --> 00:24:08.644
- Wait, I have a question that...
- <i>Procedure is complete.</i>


00:24:29.636 --> 00:24:30.971
Robert Frost.


00:24:59.875 --> 00:25:02.877
"If you're lonely when you're
alone, you're in bad company.


00:25:02.878 --> 00:25:03.962
Sartre.


00:25:04.546 --> 00:25:06.173
Jasper 'JD' Drake."


00:25:09.092 --> 00:25:13.596
"Everything is a dangerous drug
except reality, which is unendurable.


00:25:13.597 --> 00:25:16.934
Connolly. Captain
Getty Frederick. 1986."


00:25:26.985 --> 00:25:31.615
"Only those who will risk going too far
can possibly find out how far one can go.


00:25:32.241 --> 00:25:33.408
T.S. Eliot.


00:25:34.868 --> 00:25:37.704
Captain Bradford Shaw. 1947."


00:27:35.322 --> 00:27:36.490
Oh, shit.


00:28:38.468 --> 00:28:41.847
<i>May you have a very long life</i>


00:28:42.389 --> 00:28:45.475
<i>We wish you</i>


00:28:45.809 --> 00:28:47.686
<i>A very</i>


00:28:48.020 --> 00:28:51.148
<i>Long life</i>


00:28:53.400 --> 00:28:58.197
<i>Hurray, hurray, hurray</i>


00:47:28.056 --> 00:47:32.728
"Only those who will risk going too far
can possibly find out how far one can go."


00:48:24.446 --> 00:48:26.615
What are you doing?


00:48:29.785 --> 00:48:30.869
Shit.


00:48:40.170 --> 00:48:41.547
Oh, my, my, my.


00:51:30.507 --> 00:51:31.592
Good evening, Drasa.


00:51:32.718 --> 00:51:34.761
Even though I'm not
supposed to be here.


00:51:35.971 --> 00:51:37.055
Good evening, Levi.


00:51:37.639 --> 00:51:40.601
And we're cloaked,
so who's watching?


00:51:44.605 --> 00:51:46.857
I made rabbit pie.


00:51:47.983 --> 00:51:49.151
Do you like rabbit pie?


00:51:50.777 --> 00:51:51.862
I intend to.


00:51:53.989 --> 00:51:55.069
What's that you're growing?


00:51:58.118 --> 00:51:59.244
I brought you flowers.


00:52:01.205 --> 00:52:02.289
'Course you did.


00:52:03.332 --> 00:52:04.374
Thank you.


00:52:10.297 --> 00:52:11.297
You're staring.


00:52:11.298 --> 00:52:13.634
Sorry. It's...


00:52:14.218 --> 00:52:15.302
Yes?


00:52:18.430 --> 00:52:21.517
There's a lot more green in
your eyes than I was expecting.


00:52:25.646 --> 00:52:26.980
You smell.


00:52:28.273 --> 00:52:29.273
Terribly.


00:52:31.151 --> 00:52:32.151
I know.


00:52:32.152 --> 00:52:33.569
I underestimated the cable sag.


00:52:33.570 --> 00:52:35.363
I had to do the
back half by hand.


00:52:35.364 --> 00:52:38.533
Yeah. I don't think I can allow
you to come in smelling this way.


00:52:38.534 --> 00:52:41.411
Why don't you go wash up
quick at the bathhouse?


00:52:41.954 --> 00:52:44.715
I'll set out some fresh clothes from
my predecessors outside the door.


00:53:47.853 --> 00:53:53.107
Yukon? Siberia? Remote
Scandinavia, maybe?


00:53:53.108 --> 00:53:54.817
I don't know. They
sedated me on the flight.


00:53:54.818 --> 00:53:57.154
- I'm not sure how long I was out.
- Same.


00:53:57.863 --> 00:53:59.864
It's somewhere in the far
northern hemisphere though.


00:53:59.865 --> 00:54:00.948
I know that much.


00:54:00.949 --> 00:54:02.408
How can you be so
sure about that?


00:54:02.409 --> 00:54:03.869
The seasons.


00:54:04.578 --> 00:54:06.162
It was early fall when
I left the States.


00:54:06.163 --> 00:54:07.483
It was still fall
when I arrived.


00:54:08.290 --> 00:54:09.291
Military?


00:54:10.667 --> 00:54:11.667
Marines.


00:54:11.668 --> 00:54:12.627
Former.


00:54:12.628 --> 00:54:14.880
What's the longest kill
shot you've ever made?


00:54:15.881 --> 00:54:17.298
Don't say that you don't know.


00:54:17.299 --> 00:54:19.509
Every top-shelf sniper knows
the distance of every ticket


00:54:19.510 --> 00:54:21.302
they've ever
punched, so come on.


00:54:21.303 --> 00:54:22.762
3,241 meters.


00:54:22.763 --> 00:54:23.972
Thirty-two hun...


00:54:24.640 --> 00:54:25.640
A kill shot?


00:54:26.558 --> 00:54:27.809
Yeah.


00:54:29.895 --> 00:54:30.979
That would put you in...


00:54:31.730 --> 00:54:32.814
Top five in the world.


00:54:33.982 --> 00:54:36.902
Did you make that impossible
shot in Yemen, May of last year?


00:54:39.696 --> 00:54:41.072
I did not participate in,


00:54:41.073 --> 00:54:44.200
nor do I have any knowledge of, any
operation in Yemen in May of last year.


00:54:44.201 --> 00:54:48.246
Rumor was it was windy, 25 knots
east to west, with gusts of 40.


00:54:48.247 --> 00:54:51.082
That would have been a
very, very good shot.


00:54:51.083 --> 00:54:53.000
3,800 meters.


00:54:53.001 --> 00:54:54.001
World record.


00:54:54.503 --> 00:54:56.421
I'd kiss the ring of
whoever made that shot.


00:54:57.714 --> 00:54:58.882
Too bad it wasn't you.


00:55:02.845 --> 00:55:03.845
What?


00:55:07.349 --> 00:55:10.268
I've been staring at this gorge
every day for the last six months.


00:55:10.269 --> 00:55:14.982
And I gotta say, the view
is much better over here.


00:55:18.777 --> 00:55:20.695
You know what I keep thinking
about, night after night,


00:55:20.696 --> 00:55:22.488
while I sit over there
on that platform?


00:55:22.489 --> 00:55:24.241
How you're gonna
get in my pants?


00:55:30.414 --> 00:55:31.664
Well, after that.


00:55:31.665 --> 00:55:33.291
Yes, after that, sorry.


00:55:33.292 --> 00:55:35.586
Please, tell me. What have
you been thinking about?


00:55:37.713 --> 00:55:39.298
What's the truth
about this place?


00:55:40.257 --> 00:55:42.801
What's the truth about those
Hollow Men down in the Gorge?


00:55:44.094 --> 00:55:45.220
You know,


00:55:46.680 --> 00:55:49.224
a long time ago,
before I was born,


00:55:50.475 --> 00:55:51.685
my father was KGB.


00:55:52.311 --> 00:55:56.315
And years later, when I was a
child, he would say to me...


00:55:57.983 --> 00:56:01.653
"Drasa, my Little Lion, you
don't want to know the truth.


00:56:02.613 --> 00:56:03.988
It's better if you don't know."


00:56:03.989 --> 00:56:06.366
And I would bitch and
whine, and say, "Why, Daddy?


00:56:07.075 --> 00:56:08.619
Why don't I want
to know the truth?"


00:56:11.205 --> 00:56:12.205
What did he say?


00:56:12.998 --> 00:56:14.249
He would say,


00:56:14.958 --> 00:56:17.960
"Because too much truth
puts sadness in your heart


00:56:17.961 --> 00:56:20.005
and madness in your mind."


00:56:20.923 --> 00:56:21.924
I don't know.


00:56:23.467 --> 00:56:25.802
In my experience, it's hiding
the truth that does that.


00:56:26.720 --> 00:56:28.013
And when did you learn that?


00:56:30.766 --> 00:56:32.142
First time I pulled the trigger.


00:56:34.019 --> 00:56:35.062
Will you tell me about it?


00:56:39.399 --> 00:56:40.566
It was just outside of Belize,


00:56:40.567 --> 00:56:43.153
and I was on a fishing
boat two klicks away.


00:56:45.322 --> 00:56:48.784
I've had the same recurring
nightmare about it ever since.


00:56:50.369 --> 00:56:51.409
Who have you told this to?


00:56:53.455 --> 00:56:54.455
Just you.


00:56:56.500 --> 00:56:58.210
Why did you choose
this profession?


00:57:03.757 --> 00:57:06.635
Hunting was just a part of my
homeschooling growing up in Oregon,


00:57:07.261 --> 00:57:11.682
and my dad, he was the
best instructor I ever had.


00:57:13.141 --> 00:57:14.141
He loved it.


00:57:15.227 --> 00:57:16.311
He made me love it.


00:57:16.812 --> 00:57:17.938
Love what exactly?


00:57:19.314 --> 00:57:20.941
The art of the perfect shot.


00:57:24.611 --> 00:57:25.611
Yeah.


00:57:25.946 --> 00:57:26.947
Do you still love it?


00:57:27.447 --> 00:57:28.615
Not like I did.


00:57:30.450 --> 00:57:35.372
I can't compartmentalize
the way I used to.


00:57:37.958 --> 00:57:39.710
My father always
heard my secrets.


00:57:40.836 --> 00:57:42.212
I didn't have to bury them.


00:57:46.383 --> 00:57:51.805
You bury enough secrets, the
graveyard runs out of room.


00:57:58.520 --> 00:58:01.190
You dragged your mattress up the
stairs and made your bed here.


00:58:02.399 --> 00:58:03.650
For tactical reasons.


00:58:04.401 --> 00:58:05.569
I did the same thing.


01:00:03.729 --> 01:00:05.063
Did you lie to me, Levi?


01:00:05.981 --> 01:00:07.191
About what?


01:00:08.692 --> 01:00:10.152
Being a terrible dancer.


01:00:12.654 --> 01:00:13.822
Maybe a little bit.


01:01:10.087 --> 01:01:11.088
There.


01:01:11.588 --> 01:01:13.882
Those three close together.


01:01:15.217 --> 01:01:16.593
Orion's Belt.


01:01:17.427 --> 01:01:18.428
I see it.


01:01:19.388 --> 01:01:22.266
He told me to look at the
Hunter on Valentine's Day


01:01:22.766 --> 01:01:24.560
knowing that he had ended it.


01:01:25.185 --> 01:01:26.270
I'm sorry.


01:01:30.816 --> 01:01:34.278
What do you do when the
sadness overwhelms you?


01:01:36.822 --> 01:01:39.575
Sometimes I'll read a poem.


01:01:42.619 --> 01:01:44.121
Maybe try and write one.


01:01:45.205 --> 01:01:46.373
You write poetry?


01:01:48.041 --> 01:01:49.293
Almost every day.


01:01:50.711 --> 01:01:52.004
Seriously?


01:01:53.380 --> 01:01:54.882
I even took a class.


01:01:55.757 --> 01:01:59.344
Wednesday nights, 4:00 to 7:00
p.m., at Mesa Community College.


01:02:00.637 --> 01:02:03.515
Well, are you talented?


01:02:04.266 --> 01:02:05.516
No, I'm terrible.


01:02:05.517 --> 01:02:07.686
Sure. Like you're
a terrible dancer?


01:02:08.187 --> 01:02:09.479
Yeah.


01:02:09.980 --> 01:02:11.899
Will you write me
a terrible poem?


01:02:12.774 --> 01:02:14.109
Maybe I already have.


01:02:15.527 --> 01:02:16.695
Recite it for me.


01:02:17.487 --> 01:02:19.698
- Absolutely not.
- Oh, come on.


01:02:20.616 --> 01:02:21.949
No chance in hell.


01:02:21.950 --> 01:02:23.826
- At least tell me the title?
- No.


01:02:23.827 --> 01:02:25.620
Well, then I don't believe you.


01:02:25.621 --> 01:02:27.830
You haven't written a terrible
poem for me, have you?


01:02:27.831 --> 01:02:29.207
I have.


01:02:29.208 --> 01:02:30.625
But I just started it.


01:02:30.626 --> 01:02:32.461
Then tell me the title.


01:02:34.171 --> 01:02:37.049
- It's a working title.
- Tell me the working title.


01:02:40.427 --> 01:02:42.221
"She Collapsed the Night."


01:02:49.186 --> 01:02:50.229
It's that bad?


01:02:50.979 --> 01:02:51.980
I love it.


01:02:53.815 --> 01:02:55.859
Shit. I love it.


01:02:56.485 --> 01:02:58.194
No, you have to tell me.


01:02:58.195 --> 01:03:00.071
- Come on. Please. Please.
- There's no...


01:03:00.072 --> 01:03:01.657
That's not happening.


01:03:05.285 --> 01:03:06.786
Did you like the rabbit pie?


01:03:06.787 --> 01:03:07.871
No.


01:03:09.206 --> 01:03:11.041
I fucking loved the rabbit pie.


01:03:33.397 --> 01:03:34.565
No!


01:03:36.775 --> 01:03:37.901
Levi!


01:06:31.825 --> 01:06:34.076
Don't touch it. It's
some kind of adhesive.


01:06:34.077 --> 01:06:35.162
Okay.


01:06:37.122 --> 01:06:38.122
You came for me.


01:06:39.333 --> 01:06:40.918
Like you wouldn't do the same.


01:06:44.463 --> 01:06:46.590
- What is this place?
- I don't know.


01:06:47.216 --> 01:06:49.258
Please tell me you
brought an auto ascender.


01:06:49.259 --> 01:06:50.469
Of course I did.


01:06:50.969 --> 01:06:53.263
Let's head to the east
wall and find the cable.


01:07:21.208 --> 01:07:22.209
Drasa.


01:08:12.676 --> 01:08:14.011
- You good?
- Yeah.


01:08:15.095 --> 01:08:16.555
What do you think they wanted?


01:08:17.264 --> 01:08:21.435
Given how emaciated they are, my
guess is that to them we're food.


01:08:22.560 --> 01:08:23.769
One of them rode off.


01:08:23.770 --> 01:08:25.314
Yeah, I saw that.


01:08:30.319 --> 01:08:31.277
No.


01:08:31.278 --> 01:08:32.946
- What?
- The auto ascender.


01:08:34.531 --> 01:08:39.077
Must have fallen out in the river,
and it's 500 meters to the top.


01:08:42.080 --> 01:08:43.290
We're stuck here.


01:08:49.421 --> 01:08:50.671
We follow the river south.


01:08:51.423 --> 01:08:53.300
Has to drain out of
the Gorge somewhere.


01:08:55.551 --> 01:08:56.845
It's a military uniform.


01:08:59.473 --> 01:09:02.308
Old military. First
Airborne American.


01:09:02.309 --> 01:09:05.686
I saw British SAS and a
Soviet Spetsnaz back there.


01:09:05.687 --> 01:09:06.897
Postwar.


01:09:10.192 --> 01:09:12.694
All these uniforms
are from the 1940s.


01:09:15.656 --> 01:09:17.115
Cavalry on horseback.


01:09:17.783 --> 01:09:19.660
They're the lost battalions.


01:09:20.953 --> 01:09:23.037
They should be long dead, Levi.


01:09:25.207 --> 01:09:26.500
We should keep moving.


01:10:07.165 --> 01:10:09.458
<i>"This is the way the world ends.</i>


01:10:09.459 --> 01:10:12.004
<i>Not with a bang but a whimper."</i>


01:10:13.172 --> 01:10:17.759
<i>It's from the T.S. Eliot poem about people
stuck in a world between life and death.</i>


01:10:18.677 --> 01:10:20.511
<i>It's called</i> "The Hollow Men."


01:10:20.512 --> 01:10:22.097
The Hollow Men.


01:10:24.016 --> 01:10:25.058
Yeah.


01:11:17.110 --> 01:11:18.904
This damage looks seismic.


01:11:19.530 --> 01:11:20.989
Earthquake maybe.


01:13:10.891 --> 01:13:11.934
Cyanide.


01:13:12.976 --> 01:13:14.645
They chose to do it themselves.


01:13:17.606 --> 01:13:18.607
What's worse than death?


01:13:19.358 --> 01:13:20.776
This place is evil.


01:15:31.573 --> 01:15:33.075
Making a hole!


01:15:49.633 --> 01:15:53.011
Shit. They're everywhere.
We're too exposed.


01:15:54.179 --> 01:15:55.264
The Gorge wall.


01:16:00.477 --> 01:16:01.644
Levi.


01:16:01.645 --> 01:16:03.187
We get boxed in, we're screwed.


01:16:03.188 --> 01:16:04.648
We're screwed anyway.


01:16:09.987 --> 01:16:11.029
Barricade.


01:18:35.257 --> 01:18:36.258
Levi.


01:18:43.182 --> 01:18:44.724
It's a backup generator.


01:18:44.725 --> 01:18:47.227
Propane remains stable
indefinitely, so...


01:19:18.550 --> 01:19:23.305
<i>It is July 12th or 13th, 1946.</i>


01:19:24.264 --> 01:19:25.890
<i>Our community here was formed</i>


01:19:25.891 --> 01:19:28.810
<i>as part of a top secret coalition
of nations from both East and West.</i>


01:19:29.686 --> 01:19:31.395
<i>During the last years
of World War II,</i>


01:19:31.396 --> 01:19:33.648
<i>while Robert Oppenheimer
and his Los Alamos community</i>


01:19:33.649 --> 01:19:34.815
<i>developed the atom bomb,</i>


01:19:34.816 --> 01:19:38.445
<i>we were developing similarly
destructive biochemical missiles.</i>


01:19:39.196 --> 01:19:43.074
<i>Six days ago, an 8.1 earthquake
struck this location,</i>


01:19:43.075 --> 01:19:46.202
<i>severely compromising the
integrity of our facility.</i>


01:19:46.203 --> 01:19:51.124
<i>Our duty here is no longer
about research, but containment.</i>


01:19:54.711 --> 01:19:57.171
<i>We are working around the clock</i>


01:19:57.172 --> 01:19:59.883
<i>to ensure this toxin
doesn't escape the Gorge.</i>


01:20:01.301 --> 01:20:03.469
<i>Exposure to the
biochemical contaminant</i>


01:20:03.470 --> 01:20:08.057
<i>has literally merged the genetic
DNA of the biological entities</i>


01:20:08.058 --> 01:20:09.393
<i>in our gorge environment.</i>


01:20:09.977 --> 01:20:15.774
<i>Human DNA has merged with
plants, animals and even insects.</i>


01:20:17.651 --> 01:20:20.862
<i>Some people are more resistant
to contamination than others,</i>


01:20:20.863 --> 01:20:24.283
<i>especially if exposure is
limited to hours instead of days.</i>


01:20:25.367 --> 01:20:29.413
<i>If infected, mutations will
begin to appear within five days.</i>


01:20:29.913 --> 01:20:33.125
<i>They will present themselves
physically, like this.</i>


01:20:36.670 --> 01:20:40.173
<i>Our strategic forethought in
choosing this isolated location</i>


01:20:40.174 --> 01:20:43.718
<i>is the only factor that may
possibly save the rest of humankind</i>


01:20:43.719 --> 01:20:45.971
<i>from the fate that we
have sealed for ourselves.</i>


01:20:47.514 --> 01:20:48.765
<i>I'm so sorry.</i>


01:20:49.474 --> 01:20:51.602
<i>May God have mercy on our souls.</i>


01:21:00.360 --> 01:21:03.738
Sounds like we could be fine if
our exposure is limited to hours.


01:21:03.739 --> 01:21:06.325
Well, let's find a
way out quick then.


01:21:07.534 --> 01:21:08.534
What?


01:21:09.620 --> 01:21:10.954
Maybe a way out.


01:21:19.588 --> 01:21:21.507
That's not from the 1940s.


01:21:22.174 --> 01:21:23.217
Late 2000s.


01:21:24.718 --> 01:21:26.677
Why not just send in
a bomber squadron?


01:21:26.678 --> 01:21:28.764
Erase this whole mess
and call it a day.


01:21:30.891 --> 01:21:33.143
"Darklake." Paramilitary.


01:21:34.102 --> 01:21:35.269
They haven't bombed the Gorge


01:21:35.270 --> 01:21:37.189
because they're still
studying what's in it.


01:21:38.899 --> 01:21:40.776
We're not working
for the military.


01:21:45.322 --> 01:21:47.491
They used all this to set
up their research drones.


01:21:48.784 --> 01:21:52.621
Darklake is a huge corporation
specializing in genetic research.


01:21:54.706 --> 01:21:57.501
Their drones are collecting
hybrid DNA samples.


01:21:58.460 --> 01:22:00.128
They're building super soldiers.


01:22:01.046 --> 01:22:02.840
That's the mother
of all secrets.


01:22:03.507 --> 01:22:06.175
Young soldiers and scientists
studied like suffering lab rats.


01:22:06.176 --> 01:22:08.678
Private defense contractors
have been researching


01:22:08.679 --> 01:22:11.265
genetic soldier
enhancement for decades,


01:22:12.015 --> 01:22:14.059
and everything down here
is genetically brand-new.


01:22:15.561 --> 01:22:17.479
We're here to protect
their secrets.


01:23:01.481 --> 01:23:04.067
Before we head out, I need
to say something to you.


01:23:04.693 --> 01:23:06.068
Let me guess.


01:23:06.069 --> 01:23:07.196
It's your poem?


01:23:08.405 --> 01:23:10.073
No, it's not my poem.


01:23:13.202 --> 01:23:16.954
If something happens, and we
don't make it out of here,


01:23:16.955 --> 01:23:19.833
and this is the way the
world ends, for us anyway,


01:23:21.418 --> 01:23:22.878
to me it was worth it


01:23:24.129 --> 01:23:25.589
because I got to know you.


01:23:26.507 --> 01:23:27.883
It wasn't easy,


01:23:28.967 --> 01:23:30.511
getting to know each other.


01:23:31.011 --> 01:23:32.012
No, it wasn't.


01:23:43.023 --> 01:23:44.274
You ready for this?


01:23:46.777 --> 01:23:48.237
We go strong.


01:23:55.953 --> 01:23:59.248
My gear pack. I left it here.
It has all the ammo in it.


01:24:06.046 --> 01:24:08.090
These things can
think tactically.


01:24:23.397 --> 01:24:24.982
They're playing with us.


01:24:25.607 --> 01:24:27.526
They know we can't see a thing.


01:24:31.405 --> 01:24:32.948
Let's make it mutual.


01:25:26.293 --> 01:25:27.628
Drasa!


01:26:45.706 --> 01:26:48.208
Drasa!


01:27:32.669 --> 01:27:37.299
I'm going to cut what's
left of your ugly face off.


01:29:22.362 --> 01:29:23.447
Are you okay?


01:29:25.741 --> 01:29:27.534
- I'm okay. I'm okay.
- Yeah.


01:29:33.665 --> 01:29:35.292
"B. Shaw."


01:29:36.585 --> 01:29:37.669
Bradford.


01:29:40.756 --> 01:29:43.050
He was the first soldier
in the West Tower.


01:29:44.510 --> 01:29:46.345
He named the Hollow Men.


01:29:51.475 --> 01:29:52.475
Levi.


01:29:57.231 --> 01:29:58.315
Where are we?


01:30:07.449 --> 01:30:09.617
We're in a chemical
missile facility.


01:30:09.618 --> 01:30:11.619
I came down a missile silo.


01:30:11.620 --> 01:30:13.247
They're the only way out.


01:30:25.926 --> 01:30:29.179
The earthquake damaged the
missiles, and they started leaking.


01:30:32.057 --> 01:30:34.309
The contaminant is in the fog.


01:33:46.293 --> 01:33:47.878
I know how we're
getting out of here.


01:33:48.378 --> 01:33:50.505
These old jeeps have
powerful winches.


01:33:50.506 --> 01:33:52.508
It'll work just like
an auto ascender.


01:34:30.420 --> 01:34:31.963
Head to the eastern wall.


01:34:31.964 --> 01:34:33.549
The zip line should be close.


01:34:36.593 --> 01:34:38.262
There. That's it.


01:35:03.996 --> 01:35:05.289
I'm out.


01:36:01.803 --> 01:36:03.180
Levi.


01:36:10.979 --> 01:36:11.980
Levi!


01:36:22.741 --> 01:36:23.741
Toolbox.


01:37:22.718 --> 01:37:23.844
No!


01:37:28.515 --> 01:37:29.515
The propane!


01:38:12.518 --> 01:38:13.852
Cut the rope.


01:38:14.520 --> 01:38:15.521
Levi.


01:38:45.217 --> 01:38:46.760
It was so surreal down there.


01:38:48.929 --> 01:38:50.931
Like a waking nightmare.


01:38:53.600 --> 01:38:55.894
That's as close to hell
as I ever want to get.


01:38:58.272 --> 01:39:00.065
We'll need to quarantine.


01:39:02.359 --> 01:39:03.443
Five days.


01:39:08.365 --> 01:39:09.783
What if we're infected?


01:39:12.578 --> 01:39:14.371
I'll do what's necessary.


01:39:19.835 --> 01:39:20.878
Same.


01:39:22.504 --> 01:39:24.339
I have radio check tomorrow.


01:39:25.132 --> 01:39:26.132
Same.


01:39:26.967 --> 01:39:29.553
I don't know how I'm
supposed to get back across.


01:39:30.053 --> 01:39:32.389
There's a C19 grappling
gun in the back.


01:39:33.974 --> 01:39:35.184
That should do it.


01:39:36.059 --> 01:39:38.769
Well, I guess the Russians
stock a better armory.


01:39:38.770 --> 01:39:41.815
They also make better vodka.


01:39:42.733 --> 01:39:43.734
Here.


01:39:45.152 --> 01:39:47.237
To making it out alive.


01:39:56.079 --> 01:39:58.248
Do you know why I
even got this job?


01:39:58.790 --> 01:40:01.043
Because of that impossible
shot you made in Yemen?


01:40:02.419 --> 01:40:04.546
No, I wasn't lying about that.


01:40:05.297 --> 01:40:06.631
I didn't make that shot.


01:40:06.632 --> 01:40:07.841
I know.


01:40:08.342 --> 01:40:10.260
I know exactly who
made that shot.


01:40:13.347 --> 01:40:14.598
Why did you get the job?


01:40:16.850 --> 01:40:19.436
They chose me because
I was expendable.


01:40:20.312 --> 01:40:21.563
Expendable?


01:40:22.523 --> 01:40:23.774
No attachments.


01:40:24.274 --> 01:40:26.944
No one to miss me
if I disappeared.


01:40:29.029 --> 01:40:31.365
Nothing to live for
except the next mission.


01:40:34.576 --> 01:40:36.328
But now it's all flipped.


01:40:38.205 --> 01:40:40.290
And I have everything
to live for.


01:40:45.254 --> 01:40:46.380
We could run.


01:40:47.047 --> 01:40:50.467
I know a place in France,
and we could be safe there.


01:40:50.968 --> 01:40:52.427
For as long as we want.


01:40:53.220 --> 01:40:58.599
Drasa, I want to leave with you
more than anything in the world.


01:40:58.600 --> 01:41:00.643
But what about this place?


01:41:00.644 --> 01:41:03.271
What about the next pair of
soldiers that they bring in here,


01:41:03.272 --> 01:41:06.817
and inherit their
secrets, and their lies?


01:41:09.319 --> 01:41:11.697
And every Hollow Man
is a contaminant.


01:41:12.406 --> 01:41:13.866
So if one of them gets out...


01:41:18.412 --> 01:41:20.247
We need to destroy the Gorge.


01:41:28.130 --> 01:41:31.757
Remember, mutations will
appear within five days.


01:41:31.758 --> 01:41:35.094
So, if we make it to day
six, we're in the clear.


01:41:35.095 --> 01:41:37.180
- But if not...
- If not, we're dead.


01:41:37.181 --> 01:41:40.058
But if we're clear,
we meet up next week.


01:41:42.019 --> 01:41:43.020
We go strong.


01:41:43.604 --> 01:41:45.606
- Yes?
- Always.


01:41:49.026 --> 01:41:51.069
- Lis...
- Don't say good-bye.


01:41:52.571 --> 01:41:54.113
I don't want to
hear you say that.


01:41:54.114 --> 01:41:55.656
I wasn't going to say good-bye.


01:41:55.657 --> 01:41:58.702
Okay. And what
were you gonna say?


01:42:07.586 --> 01:42:08.879
That I love you.


01:42:15.260 --> 01:42:18.013
<i>This is West Tower performing
radio check. Do you copy?</i>


01:42:19.473 --> 01:42:21.474
I repeat, this is West Tower
performing radio check.


01:42:21.475 --> 01:42:23.392
Do you copy? Over.


01:42:23.393 --> 01:42:24.853
<i>Authentication code?</i>


01:42:25.812 --> 01:42:27.980
Delta, Theta, four, one, Omega.


01:42:27.981 --> 01:42:29.191
<i>Stand by.</i>


01:42:30.943 --> 01:42:34.363
<i>Levi? Do you know who this is?</i>


01:42:36.657 --> 01:42:37.990
Yes.


01:42:37.991 --> 01:42:41.370
Our research drone computer
system was activated.


01:42:42.412 --> 01:42:44.248
Did you go into the Gorge?


01:42:44.998 --> 01:42:48.794
<i>Negative. But I did see one of
your drones fly out of here.</i>


01:42:49.336 --> 01:42:51.672
<i>Seems like you're not
a spook after all.</i>


01:42:52.965 --> 01:42:54.465
The private sector is where


01:42:54.466 --> 01:42:58.095
the most important scientific
progress happens these days.


01:42:58.679 --> 01:43:01.347
<i>Do you know what kind
of work I do here?</i>


01:43:01.348 --> 01:43:03.350
I'm assuming the
kind that pays well.


01:43:03.934 --> 01:43:06.561
Let's just say the primary
aim of our research


01:43:06.562 --> 01:43:09.522
is to make American
ground forces unbeatable


01:43:09.523 --> 01:43:12.567
<i>against any foreign
army in the world.</i>


01:43:12.568 --> 01:43:16.113
I'm sure you can appreciate what we
could do with a military like that.


01:43:17.906 --> 01:43:19.116
Absolutely.


01:43:21.577 --> 01:43:27.541
Levi, have you noticed any movement
from your eastern counterpart?


01:43:31.670 --> 01:43:32.671
Negative.


01:43:33.297 --> 01:43:37.426
<i>Because if it wasn't you that activated
our computer system in the Gorge,</i>


01:43:38.010 --> 01:43:40.637
I have to assume that it was
your eastern counterpart.


01:43:42.347 --> 01:43:45.601
<i>There are, after all,
only the two of you there.</i>


01:43:48.228 --> 01:43:50.772
<i>You are to neutralize
your counterpart.</i>


01:43:52.733 --> 01:43:54.151
<i>Immediately.</i>


01:43:55.152 --> 01:43:56.612
<i>Do you understand?</i>


01:43:58.363 --> 01:43:59.906
Consider it done.


01:43:59.907 --> 01:44:03.243
<i>Copy that. Thank you, Levi.</i>


01:44:23.722 --> 01:44:27.808
Commander, Levi
Kane is compromised.


01:44:27.809 --> 01:44:30.228
Gather your team. We'll
leave in the morning.


01:44:30.229 --> 01:44:32.146
<i>You're coming with us, ma'am?</i>


01:44:32.147 --> 01:44:33.732
He's my mistake.


01:44:34.608 --> 01:44:37.027
I'll kill him
myself if I have to.


01:46:00.235 --> 01:46:01.486
Run!


01:46:34.686 --> 01:46:37.104
There's no sign of Levi
Kane anywhere in the tower


01:46:37.105 --> 01:46:39.148
or on the surrounding compound.


01:46:39.149 --> 01:46:40.859
What if he decided to run?


01:46:43.737 --> 01:46:45.196
Raise the quadcopters.


01:46:45.197 --> 01:46:47.406
There's no sign of the
counterpart either.


01:46:47.407 --> 01:46:50.452
If Levi didn't keep his post, why
believe that he would have killed her?


01:46:52.454 --> 01:46:53.622
Split them up.


01:46:54.122 --> 01:46:56.667
Drone protocol,
quadcopters, verification...


01:49:25.816 --> 01:49:27.734
Commander, what's
that on the wall?


01:49:56.430 --> 01:49:59.433
"Three things cannot
be long hidden:


01:50:00.225 --> 01:50:04.771
the sun, the moon and the truth.


01:50:06.273 --> 01:50:07.273
Buddha.


01:50:09.568 --> 01:50:11.028
Levi Kane."


01:50:45.354 --> 01:50:46.772
What the hell was that?


01:51:08.585 --> 01:51:12.381
The cloakers. He's
rigged the cloakers.


01:51:15.759 --> 01:51:17.135
The Gorge is exposed.


01:51:26.520 --> 01:51:27.980
Straydog.


01:51:30.107 --> 01:51:31.483
We have two minutes.


01:51:37.281 --> 01:51:39.408
Prepare for immediate takeoff.


01:51:54.840 --> 01:51:56.884
Get us airborne. Now!


01:52:17.821 --> 01:52:20.949
Forget altitude!
We need distance!


01:52:43.555 --> 01:52:45.057
Fast!


01:56:53.305 --> 01:56:54.680
Hello, Drasa.


01:56:54.681 --> 01:56:57.768
Hello, Levi. You're late.


01:56:58.727 --> 01:57:01.854
Sorry. I got injured
at my old job.


01:57:01.855 --> 01:57:05.316
Well, if you're looking for a
new one, the kitchen's hiring.


01:57:05.317 --> 01:57:06.735
Got any special skills?


01:57:08.237 --> 01:57:09.487
I'm a pretty good shot.


01:57:09.488 --> 01:57:10.863
How good?


01:57:10.864 --> 01:57:12.824
Last one was 3,900 meters.


01:57:13.617 --> 01:57:15.410
Had to beat my record.


01:57:17.037 --> 01:57:18.497
I had to get back to you.
